## Three important things before you start

- Confirm the cash arrangement: Is there one shared physical கல்லா for all three sectors, or does each sector have a separate cash box? This affects the reconciliation database and workflow.
- Use real business rules: The actual service-to-sector mapping, pricing, discounts, tax settings, employee permissions, and opening cash balance must be configured with the owner. Do not invent them.
- Protect your first project: Use a separate development database and test financial workflows with fictional transactions before putting real business records into production.

One final recommendation: make the dashboard visually impressive, but make the billing screen exceptionally fast. The owner may be attracted by the design, but the operator will judge the software by how quickly and reliably it handles customers. That combination is what will make this project stand out.